A||||0||roadrunner||Gas Smell/Leak  Solved||||1||
Z||000000||roadrunner||02-19-2000||10:52 PM||||<BR>My '86 SE V-6 gave off a heavy ordor of gasoline, but my searching found no leaking fuel lines.  Finally I found after driving the car 10 miles, a puddle of gasoline about 1/4 inch deep was in the cavity surrounding # 3 & 5 fuel injectors.  In fact, gasoline was bubbling up from the head at the bottom of  # 3 injector.  I replaced #3 and the problem was solved.  The way injectors are built enables them to  leak above the O ring causing gasoline to exit the engine.   If anyone has a strong gas smell and can't find why, check your injectors.   A clue was that the area around the leaky injector was very clean as the gas had washed away the oil which had collected on the engine.  Since the injectors are under the plenum chamber, it is not easy to see the leak.   Hope this helps someone else.||||reg||1
